From 452f33c7969da241ea74bf2943add9b623618300 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 04:13:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/24] Make kernel walk validation reachable, and say where it
 stands

On macOS 27 a captured root never validated: every mapper read a resolve
sampled came from its first sixteen reads, one object's page, and the
crossing probe ran once per resolve at the end of that page, so distinct
pages and a non-zero crossing never came. Strict then refused every
type-11 resolve for the whole boot.

A reader validating a root now also samples the first read of each new
kernel page it touches, up to eight, with a crossing probe at the end of
each while one is still owed. And a capture now reads VBAR_EL1 and, while
the root has not validated, takes one round of sandwiched probes of
kernel text from there per mapper publish, up to eight rounds per root.
VBAR is only an entry point: a probe counts only if every CPU read
succeeds and the sandwich is stable.

The bar is not lower but stricter. A sample qualifies only if it holds a
non-zero byte and the walk resolved it through level-3 page descriptors,
the ones the mapper's objects live under; text mapped by blocks is logged
and counts for nothing. Of eight qualifying samples, four must be the
mapper's own reads, over three pages, with one crossing between two
level-3 leaves.

kva_walk_validation_state reports every condition by name every ten
seconds while a root validates, kva_walk_validated and kva_walk_cost
carry the same, and kva_walk_root names VBAR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 07e1bca22d374be7e3a7c5cf258fd2133cbe8b0e)
